{"name":"Shutters","hex":"#6c705e","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Shutters","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["plural of Shutter"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Shutters"}],"entries":[{"title":"Window shutter","blocks":[{"text":"A window shutter is a solid and stable window covering, usually consisting of a frame of vertical stiles and horizontal rails. Set within this frame can be louvers, solid panels, fabric, glass and almost any other item that can be mounted within a frame.\nShutters may be employed for a variety of reasons, including controlling the amount of sunlight that enters a room, to provide privacy, security, to protect against weather or unwanted intrusion or damage and to enhance the aesthetics of a building."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a6/Interior-Shutters.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Window_shutter","wikidata":"Q1096423"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/Window_shutters.png/500px-Window_shutters.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/Window_shutters.png/500px-Window_shutters.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Modern interior wooden window shutters","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWindow_shutters.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Workers_installing_shutters.jpg/500px-Workers_installing_shutters.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Workers_installing_shutters.jpg/1280px-Workers_installing_shutters.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/th